{0 Preprocessing flags}

The [html_of_jsx.ppx] preprocessor transforms JSX syntax into efficient HTML rendering code, validating attributes and their types at compile time.

Pass flags after [html_of_jsx.ppx] in your dune [(preprocess ...)] stanza.

{1 [-htmx]}

Enables htmx attributes ([hx_get], [hx_post], [hx_swap], ...) and extension-specific attributes ([sse_connect], [ws_send], ...) on all HTML elements.

{@dune[
(preprocess (pps html_of_jsx.ppx -htmx))
]}

Requires the [html_of_jsx.htmx] library for the [<Htmx />] script loader. See {{!page-"HTMX-mode"}HTMX mode}.

{1 [-alpinejs]}

Enables {{:https://alpinejs.dev}Alpine.js} directives on all HTML and SVG elements: [x_data], [x_init], [x_show], [x_text], [x_html], [x_model], [x_modelable], [x_for], [x_if], [x_effect], [x_ignore], [x_ref], [x_cloak], [x_teleport], [x_id], [x_transition] and [x_transition_enter] (with [_start], [_end] and the [leave] variants).

[x_on_<event>] renders [x-on:<event>] for common DOM events ([x_on_click], [x_on_input], [x_on_keydown], [x_on_submit], ...). [x_bind_<attribute>] renders [x-bind:<attribute>] for common attributes ([x_bind_class], [x_bind_style], [x_bind_value], [x_bind_disabled], ...). The full lists are in [ppx/extra_alpinejs.ml]. Custom event names, modifiers such as [.prevent], and the [@] and [:] shorthands are not supported.

{@dune[
(preprocess (pps html_of_jsx.ppx -alpinejs))
]}

{1 [-react]}

Enables React DOM aliases: [className] maps to [class] and [htmlFor] maps to [for]. Useful as a migration bridge from React/Reason-React codebases.

{@dune[
(preprocess (pps html_of_jsx.ppx -react))
]}

See {{!page-"React-compatibility"}React compatibility}.

{1 [-disable-static-opt]}

Disables compile-time static analysis and optimization. Every element falls back to the generic [JSX.node] constructor. Useful for debugging the ppx output.

{@dune[
(preprocess (pps html_of_jsx.ppx -disable-static-opt))
]}

For details on what the static optimization does, see {{!page-"how-ppx-works"}How the ppx works}.
